    "body": "In Java this class extends java.lang.RuntimeException, as do the four other exceptions of the same package. Those four were ported onto std::runtime_error; this one was bound to the Keyple class of the same name instead, keyple::core::util::cpp::exception::RuntimeException.\r\n\r\nThat single line is the only dependency of the whole Keypop C++ API surface on Keyple, a dependency Java does not have and no CMakeLists declares. It also made this header the only one of the 151 that cannot be compiled without keyple-util on the include path, which the repository never notices because no unit test includes it.\r\n\r\nThe consequence at runtime is worse than the layering. Keyple's RuntimeException derives from Keyple's own Exception, so the two families meet only at std::exception: a caller catching std::runtime_error to handle the exceptions of this API caught the four siblings and missed precisely the one reporting an invalid signature.\r\n\r\nThe constructor signatures are unchanged, both call sites in keyple-card-calypso-crypto-legacysam-cpp-lib keep compiling.",
